@startuml
' Email claim intake: workflow and agents. Keep in sync with docs/design/email-claim-intake.md (Architecture).
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam PackageBackgroundColor #FAFBFD
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7
skinparam ArrowColor #4A6FA5
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor<<LLM>> #E3F2FD
  BorderColor<<LLM>> #1565C0
  BackgroundColor<<no LLM>> #F1F8E9
  BorderColor<<no LLM>> #558B2F
  BackgroundColor<<step>> #FFF8E1
  BorderColor<<step>> #B28704
  BackgroundColor<<app>> #FFFFFF
}

title Email claim intake: workflow and agents

actor Customer
actor "Claims processor" as CP
component "GreenMail\n(SMTP + IMAP)" as GM <<app>>
database "PostgreSQL\nclaims, photos;\nFlow: running and waiting runs" as DB

package "Parasol app" {
  component "ClaimsInboxWatcher\nIMAP IDLE; records the Message-ID,\nmoves the email to processing" as W <<app>>
  component "ClaimIntakeStarter\nskips auto-replies, self-sent mail\nand duplicates; matches the claim\nand checks the sender (code);\nkeeps a claim's emails in order;\nstarts one run (doesn't wait)" as S <<app>>
  component "Failure listener\nfailed run → failed folder,\nprocessing-problem reply" as FL <<app>>
  component "Review REST API\nPOST /api/db/claims/{id}/review-decisions\nchecks the run is waiting;\npublishes REVIEW_DECIDED" as RR <<app>>
  component "IntakeReplySender\nQute templates" as RS <<app>>

  package "ClaimIntakeFlow: one quarkus-flow workflow per email (steps do the side effects)" as FLOW {
    component "wrong sender?\n→ no-matching-claim reply" as F1 <<step>>
    component "runAgents" as F2 <<step>>
    component "policy check\n(code)" as F3 <<step>>
    component "supersede: cancel the\nclaim's waiting run" as F3b <<step>>
    component "save claim\nand photos" as F4 <<step>>
    component "reply" as F5 <<step>>
    component "file the email" as F6 <<step>>
    component "wait for review\n(listen)" as F7 <<step>>
    component "apply decision\n(switch): Ready /\nNeeds more information" as F8 <<step>>

    package "ClaimsMailboxAgent: agentic root (sequence), returns IntakeOutcome" as ROOT {
      component "EmailClassifierAgent\nemail → email type" as C <<LLM>>

      package "EmailRouter (conditional)\nmatched claim first, then email type" as ROUTER {
        package "ClaimExtractionWorkflow (parallel)\n→ claim extraction" as EX {
          component "ClaimSummaryAgent\n→ summary" as SUM <<LLM>>
          component "ClaimSentimentAgent\n→ sentiment" as SEN <<LLM>>
          component "IncidentDetailsAgent\n→ description, date, time,\nlocation, category, policy number" as DET <<LLM>>
        }
        component "ClaimFollowUpAgent\nstatus answer;\nread-only status tool" as FU <<LLM>>
        component "UnmatchedEmailAgent\nnot a claim /\nno matching claim" as NAC <<no LLM>>
      }
    }
  }
}

Customer --> GM : email (Roundcube)
GM --> W : new mail
W --> S
S --> F1 : start a run (Message-ID,\nmatched claim, sender check,\nconversation id)
F1 --> F2
F2 --> ROOT : email, matched claim (or none),\nclaim history
C --> ROUTER : email type
ROUTER --> EX : matched pending claim,\nor no match + new claim
ROUTER --> FU : matched claim\nin any other status
ROUTER --> NAC : no match +\nnot a claim or follow-up
F2 --> F3 : IntakeOutcome
F3 --> F3b
F3b --> F4
F4 --> F5
F5 --> F6
F6 --> F7 : complete claims only
F7 --> F8
F4 --> DB
F5 --> RS
F8 --> RS : thank-you /\nmissing information
F8 --> DB : claim status
RS --> GM : reply (SMTP)
FLOW ..> DB : Flow persists each run
FLOW ..> FL : run failed
FL --> RS

CP --> RR : Ready /\nNeeds more information
RR ..> F7 : REVIEW_DECIDED\n(for this claim)
RR --> DB : lock the claim;\nis the run waiting?

legend right
  |= Colour |= Meaning |
  |<#FFF8E1> | workflow step (side effects allowed) |
  |<#E3F2FD> | agent that calls the LLM (claim-intake model) |
  |<#F1F8E9> | agent with no LLM call |
  Agents have no side effects and never pause.
  Every LLM agent runs without chat memory or RAG.
  Composite agents (sequence, conditional, parallel)
  make no LLM call themselves; Flow runs each one
  as its own sub-workflow.
endlegend
@enduml
